@startuml OpenH264_Sequence_Diagram

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

title OpenH264 Example Project

actor "Application" as APP
participant "Image Task\n(image_thread_entry)" as TASK
participant "OpenH264 EP\n(openh264_ep)" as EP
participant "OpenH264 Decoder" as DEC
participant "LCDC Driver" as LCDC
participant "MIPI-DSI Driver" as MIPI
participant "ILI9881 Panel" as LCD

legend top left
**loop**  : Repeated decoding per frame  
**opt**   : Optional / conditional flow  
**note**  : Key design explanation
endlegend

== System Initialization ==

APP -> TASK: Create / start FreeRTOS task

TASK -> LCDC: R_LCDC_Open()
TASK -> LCDC: R_LCDC_Start()

TASK -> MIPI: R_MIPI_DSI_B_Open()
TASK -> LCD: ili9881_init()
note over LCD, MIPI #FFF9C4
ILI9881 initialized via
MIPI DSI commands
end note
TASK -> MIPI: R_MIPI_DSI_B_Start()

TASK -> LCDC: Display splash image

== H.264 Decoder Initialization ==

TASK -> EP: h264_start_decode_task()
EP -> DEC: WelsCreateDecoder()
EP -> DEC: Initialize(decParam)

note over DEC #D4E6F1
Decoder initialized
with default parameters
end note

== Decode and Display Loop ==

loop For each video cycle
    TASK -> EP: h264_decode_task(h264_data)

    EP -> EP: parse_annexb()
    note right of EP
    Split Annex-B stream
    into NAL units
    end note

    loop For each NAL unit
        EP -> DEC: DecodeFrameNoDelay(NAL)
        DEC --> EP: YUV420 frame
    end loop

    opt Frame ready to display
        EP -> TASK: lcd_draw_yuv(Y, U, V)

        TASK -> LCDC: Update framebuffer
        LCDC -> LCDC: YUV → RGB conversion
        LCDC -> MIPI: Video data stream
        MIPI -> LCD: Display frame
    end opt
end loop

== Frame Timing and Sync ==

LCDC -> TASK: Frame end interrupt
note over TASK
Used for FPS statistics
and timing control
end note

== Decoder Stop (Optional) ==

opt Stop playback
    TASK -> EP: h264_stop_decode_task()
    EP -> DEC: Uninitialize()
    EP -> DEC: WelsDestroyDecoder()
end opt

@enduml
